2. INSTALL RUFF IN VS CODE
============================================================

You can integrate Ruff directly into Visual Studio Code using its official extension.

2.1 Step 1: Open VS Code

Open Visual Studio Code on your computer.

2.2 Step 2: Open the Extensions Panel

Use the following keyboard shortcut:

Windows / Linux:

    Ctrl + Shift + X

Mac:

    Cmd + Shift + X

Alternatively, click the Extensions icon in the VS Code sidebar.

2.3 Step 3: Search for Ruff

Search for:

    Ruff

2.4 Step 4: Install the Official Extension

Install the official Ruff extension published by Astral.

The extension provides:

- Python linting
- Python formatting
- Import sorting
- Code diagnostics
- Automatic fixes
- Editor integration

NOTE:

The Ruff extension can cover many common use cases previously handled by separate tools such as:

- Black: Python code formatting
- isort: Import sorting
- Flake8 and selected Pylint checks: Linting

However, Ruff does not provide every feature of these tools.

============================================================
3. ENABLE FORMAT ON SAVE
============================================================

One of the most useful features in VS Code is automatic formatting when you save a Python file.

This means you do not need to format your code manually every time.

3.1 Step 1: Open VS Code Settings

Use the following keyboard shortcut:

Windows / Linux:

    Ctrl + ,

Mac:

    Cmd + ,

This opens the VS Code Settings panel.

3.2 Step 2: Enable Format On Save

Search for:

    Format On Save

Find the setting:

    Editor: Format On Save

Enable the checkbox.

Now VS Code can automatically format files when you save them.

3.3 Step 3: Set Ruff as the Default Formatter

Search for:

    Default Formatter

Select the Ruff extension as the default formatter.

You can also configure it directly in your VS Code settings.json file.

Example:

    {
        "editor.formatOnSave": true,
        "[python]": {
            "editor.defaultFormatter": "charliermarsh.ruff"
        }
    }

Explanation:

1. editor.formatOnSave:
   Enables automatic formatting when a file is saved.

2. [python]:
   Applies the following editor settings specifically to Python files.

3. editor.defaultFormatter:
   Selects Ruff as the formatter for Python files.

IMPORTANT:
The extension must be installed and available for this configuration to work.

